  "name": "coinbase-burned-into-a-payee-spent-in-the-same-block",
  "description": "F12's burn arm, which no other vector and no test in this tree reaches at all. The block 10 blocks below this one paid its producer share to a 0x01 one-shot address, so the maturity ring holds (that address, 2037000000) when this block arrives; consensus permits it, because B11 admits any user address and the 0x02 requirement is a wallet-side guard rather than a rule. A RETIRE in THIS block burns that address, and F12 rolls the ring AFTER the certificate loop — so the reward is destroyed rather than credited: matured is zero and burned carries it. The ordering is the whole content. A fold that rolled the ring first would find the payee unspent (it is unspent in the pre-state here, which is what makes the two orderings distinguishable at all), credit 2037000000 to a balance cell, and report a different matured, a different burned and a different state root — committed, because this block is on an epoch boundary. docs/RUNNING.md's operator-facing claim, that the block carrying the spend is already the first block that loses money, is true only under this order.",
